* 128-RO LTspice pilot netlist: two banks of 64 ring oscillators
* Bank A: RO0-RO63; Bank B: RO64-RO127.
* Purpose: validate oscillator startup, node visibility, and frequency extraction.
* MATLAB should construct 1023 fixed, unique cross-bank comparisons.
* This file models local threshold-voltage mismatch sensitivity only unless
* the SIGMA values are supported by calibrated technology data.

.include "45nm_HP.pm"
.options plotwinsize=0 numdgt=10 reltol=1e-4 abstol=1e-12 vntol=1e-6

* User parameters
.param VDDVAL=1.0
.param VTHRESH={VDDVAL/2}
.param TSTOP=25n
.param MAXSTEP=2p
.param N_RUNS=100
.param RUN=1
.param SIGMA_LOCAL_N=46.893m
.param SIGMA_LOCAL_P=49.158m

* Inverter with local threshold-mismatch sensitivity
.subckt INV in out vdd vss params: run_step=1
MN out in vss vss nmos W=200n L=50n delvto={SIGMA_LOCAL_N*gauss(1)+0*run_step}
MP out in vdd vdd pmos W=400n L=50n delvto={SIGMA_LOCAL_P*gauss(1)+0*run_step}
.ends INV

* Seven-stage direct-feedback ring oscillator
* OUT is exposed as a top-level subcircuit pin.
.subckt RO7 OUT VDD VSS params: run_step=1
X1 OUT n2 VDD VSS INV params: run_step={run_step}
X2 n2 n3 VDD VSS INV params: run_step={run_step}
X3 n3 n4 VDD VSS INV params: run_step={run_step}
X4 n4 n5 VDD VSS INV params: run_step={run_step}
X5 n5 n6 VDD VSS INV params: run_step={run_step}
X6 n6 n7 VDD VSS INV params: run_step={run_step}
X7 n7 OUT VDD VSS INV params: run_step={run_step}
* Equal small startup/load capacitance on every RO output.
CSTART OUT VSS 1f IC=0
.ends RO7

VDD VDD 0 {VDDVAL}
VSS VSS 0 0

* 128 oscillators
* Bank A
XRO0 ro0_out VDD VSS RO7 params: run_step={RUN}
XRO1 ro1_out VDD VSS RO7 params: run_step={RUN}
XRO2 ro2_out VDD VSS RO7 params: run_step={RUN}
